@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `nii-il34-nouns`

-- Row IL-34: the provisions the row names whose text is not in the deposited sources. Each is refused BY NAME, in the words below, so that a caller (the
-- capstone, a tester) gets "needs a source" and not a number. Nothing here is an answer.
--
-- 1. The Institute's charge on a yeshiva student who has not regularised his military status (row IL-05, open question 3). The Institute's page (fetched by
--    row IL-05 on 2026-10-06, 14:51:01Z, sha256 39720f8c...125a, not deposited) says that from 1 January 2026 such a student is charged "full National
--    Insurance, without discount", 95 NIS a month more (the difference between the Schedule K item 4 and item 3 minimums). No text of any Law, regulation or order
--    in the sources says it, and the National-Civic Service Law (deposited) and s 348(e) do not turn on military status. The place of the rule is unknown.
-- 2. Amendments of the National-Civic Service Law after 2026-04-01 (the date of the deposited consolidation): see nii-s348e-civic-expiry.l4, forks C1 to C3.
-- 3. The National Insurance (Classification of Insured Persons and Determination of Employers) Order 5732-1972 s 2 ("recognised employer"); the Income Tax
--    (Deduction from Salary and Wages and Payment of Employers' Tax) Regulations 5753-1993 reg 5; the National Insurance (Collection of Insurance Contributions)
--    Regulations 5714-1954 reg 2(2): inputs of nii-s342e-several-employers.l4.
-- 4. The Minister's regulations and orders under ss 344(c), 345(b)(3), (c)(2), (f), 345B(f), 346, 349 (any order), 350(b) (the orders on the German and Dutch laws,
--    the Workers' Compensation Ordinance, the Prison Service law, the Maintenance Law), 351(k)(3): none deposited.

§ `Open items: refused by name`

@ref NOTES.md, section "Needs a source", item 1; row IL-05 open question 3
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the Institute's charge on a yeshiva student who has not regularised his military status is not in any deposited text` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Institute's charge on a yeshiva student who has not regularised his military status is not in any deposited text"

@ref NOTES.md, section "Needs a source", item 1
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the extra monthly charge on a yeshiva student who has not regularised his military status` MEANS
    `the Institute's charge on a yeshiva student who has not regularised his military status is not in any deposited text`
